# Implementation Plan - Finish OneDrive Installation

The setup for OneDrive was started but not completed in the previous session. I will finish the installation and configuration of the `onedrive` client (abraunegg/onedrive) on Ubuntu 24.04.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - You will need to authenticate the client by clicking a link and pasting the response URL back into the terminal.
> - By default, it will sync to `~/OneDrive`.

## Proposed Changes

### System Setup
1. **Add OBS Repository Key**:
   ```bash
   wget -qO - https://download.opensuse.org/repositories/home:/abraunegg/xUbuntu_24.04/Release.key | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/abraunegg-onedrive-keyring.gpg
   ```
2. **Add OBS Repository**:
   ```bash
   echo 'deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/abraunegg-onedrive-keyring.gpg] https://download.opensuse.org/repositories/home:/abraunegg/xUbuntu_24.04/ /' | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/onedrive.list
   ```
3. **Install Client**:
   ```bash
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt install onedrive
   ```

### Configuration
1. **Initial Authentication**: Run `onedrive` in a terminal. It will provide a URL; open it in a browser, log in, and paste the final response URL back into the terminal.
2. **Setup Sync Folder**: By default, it uses `~/OneDrive`.
3. **Enable Background Sync**:
   ```bash
   systemctl --user enable onedrive
   systemctl --user start onedrive
   ```

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `onedrive --display-config` to verify settings.
- Run `onedrive --display-sync-status` to check connectivity.

### Manual Verification
- Place a test file in the `~/OneDrive` folder and verify it appears on OneDrive web.
- Check the output of `journalctl --user -u onedrive` to see sync logs.
